Z||000000||Adrift||06-30-2001||03:50 PM||||I have a great idea for a spoiler for a fiero and was just wondering the process which one would go through to learn the art of fibreglass molding. Ferrarimomo, I aimed this question at you because you already seem to be doing this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Where did you learn to make fibreglass spoilers? What is required? Any good reading material/books on it you can recommend?<P>Thanks<BR>Adrift||||reg||1
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-30-2001||04:11 PM||||How to Build a Fiberglass Mold<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cstsales.com/fiberg0.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cstsales.com/fiberg0.htm</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||06-30-2001||04:17 PM||||If you were just going to make one, you might want to look into using a foam core method.. ie. make the part out of foam board, and then cover it with fiberglass.. afterwards, scoop out some of the foam and lay down more fiberglass to reinforce it. or, if it's a spoiler.. just do several layers of fiberglass on the outside. This method should be supported with steel rods inside, you can buy those at any hardware store.. just weld them together to make a stiff frame..<P>this might work, but then again it might not. I've done some work with Bondo before, but not fiberglass.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||06-30-2001||04:19 PM||||One other thing, if you use a mold release agent on the foam (I mean a lot of it), you might be able to get most of it off so you can lay down more fiberglass on the back to make a 2-sided panel, and not have one side lumpy from the remains of the foam.. just an idea.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
